  "answer": {
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "kotlin-delegation",
        "path": "src/main/kotlin/org/springframework/aot/hint/ReflectionHintsExtensions.kt",
        "start_line": 26,
        "end_line": 47,
        "quote": "inline fun <reified T> ReflectionHints.getTypeHint() =\n\tgetTypeHint(T::class.java)",
        "explanation": "All three extensions materialize the reified T as T::class.java. getTypeHint<T>() selects Java getTypeHint(Class<?>), which converts the Class to a TypeReference and performs the lookup. The customizer form selects registerType(Class<?>, Consumer<Builder>); noinline permits the bound typeHint::invoke adapter, which passes the Java Builder to the original Kotlin callback. The category form uses *memberCategories, passing the vararg elements to registerType(Class<?>, MemberCategory...), which forwards them to the TypeReference overload and TypeHint.builtWith rather than treating the array as one category."
      },
      {
        "id": "registration-class-guards",
        "path": "src/main/java/org/springframework/aot/hint/ReflectionHints.java",
        "start_line": 122,
        "end_line": 143,
        "quote": "public ReflectionHints registerType(Class<?> type, Consumer<TypeHint.Builder> typeHint) {\n\t\tAssert.notNull(type, \"'type' must not be null\");\n\t\tif (type.getCanonicalName() != null) {\n\t\t\tregisterType(TypeReference.of(type), typeHint);\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn this;\n\t}",
        "explanation": "Both Class-based registration overloads first reject a null Class with Assert.notNull, which throws IllegalArgumentException. Their only subsequent Class guard is a non-null canonical name; a Class without one is silently skipped and this is returned. Thus the customizer is not called for either a null Class or a canonical-name-less Class. For a valid Class, the appropriate TypeReference overload is reached and the customizer runs there. Primitive and array classes are not separately rejected if their canonical names are non-null."
      },
      {
        "id": "registration-state-errors",
        "path": "src/main/java/org/springframework/aot/hint/ReflectionHints.java",
        "start_line": 98,
        "end_line": 113,
        "quote": "public ReflectionHints registerType(TypeReference type, Consumer<TypeHint.Builder> typeHint) {\n\t\tBuilder builder = this.types.computeIfAbsent(type, TypeHint.Builder::new);\n\t\ttypeHint.accept(builder);\n\t\treturn this;\n\t}",
        "explanation": "Repeated registration under an equal TypeReference key—TypeReference equality is canonical-name based—reuses the same Builder. The category overload supplies TypeHint.builtWith, whose Builder.withMembers adds all categories to a HashSet: registrations therefore accumulate as set union, retaining earlier categories and collapsing duplicates. The builder is inserted by computeIfAbsent before the customizer is invoked. Because accept has no catch or rollback, a thrown exception propagates while the map entry remains; previously accumulated categories and any categories added before the throw remain. For a newly encountered type, even a throw before category mutation leaves an entry whose category set is empty."
      },
      {
        "id": "lookup-absence-errors",
        "path": "src/main/java/org/springframework/aot/hint/ReflectionHints.java",
        "start_line": 76,
        "end_line": 88,
        "quote": "public @Nullable TypeHint getTypeHint(TypeReference type) {\n\t\tBuilder typeHintBuilder = this.types.get(type);\n\t\treturn (typeHintBuilder != null ? typeHintBuilder.build() : null);\n\t}",
        "explanation": "getTypeHint(Class<?>) unconditionally calls TypeReference.of(type), then the TypeReference overload reads the map and returns null when a valid type has no entry; lookup does not create one. In contrast, registering an absent valid type creates its builder and invokes the registration callback. TypeReference.of(Class<?>) delegates to ReflectionTypeReference.of, which validates both the Class and its canonical name with Assert.notNull. Consequently lookup with null Class throws IllegalArgumentException for \"'type' must not be null\", and lookup for a Class with no canonical name throws IllegalArgumentException for \"'type.getCanonicalName()' must not be null\". Registration validates null Class directly but silently skips a non-null Class lacking a canonical name."
      },
      {
        "id": "category-snapshots",
        "path": "src/main/java/org/springframework/aot/hint/TypeHint.java",
        "start_line": 54,
        "end_line": 67,
        "quote": "private TypeHint(Builder builder) {\n\t\tthis.type = builder.type;\n\t\tthis.reachableType = builder.reachableType;\n\t\tthis.memberCategories = Set.copyOf(builder.memberCategories);",
        "explanation": "Each lookup builds a new TypeHint from the retained Builder. Set.copyOf makes that TypeHint's member-category set an unmodifiable snapshot, so a TypeHint returned earlier—and the set returned by its getMemberCategories()—does not change when the same type is registered again. A later lookup builds another TypeHint and observes the builder's newly accumulated category union."
      }
    ]
  },
